  "name": "Commander's Strike",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/targeting/crosshair-bars-yellow.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks to direct one of your companions to strike. When you do so, choose a willing creature who can see or hear you and expend one Superiority Die. That creature can immediately use its Reaction to make one attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, adding the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll on a hit.</p><section id=\"secret-0pos4GeVt9Zi2UX5\" class=\"secret\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The <strong>Directed Strike </strong>activity allows you to select the type of damage it should deal in the roll dialog.</p></section>",
